<section style="background:var(--soft)"><div class="wrap center">
  <div class="kicker">Import FAQ</div>
  <h2 class="h2">Questions about importing lectures</h2>
  <div class="faq" style="text-align:left">
    <details class="qa"><summary>What can I import?</summary><div class="a">A PDF or slide deck, photos of handwritten or printed notes, a pasted block of text, a YouTube link, or a lecture you record live inside the app. MedBank turns any of them into a full study set.</div></details>
    <details class="qa"><summary>How does the YouTube import work?</summary><div class="a">Paste the video link and MedBank reads the video's captions, then builds your note and cards from what was said. It works on public videos that have captions or subtitles.</div></details>
    <details class="qa"><summary>Can I record a lecture in class?</summary><div class="a">Yes. The recorder captures the lecture live — you can pause and resume — and afterwards it's transcribed and turned into your study set. Keep the app open with your screen on while recording.</div></details>
    <details class="qa"><summary>What exactly gets built from one import?</summary><div class="a">Always: a built note, a simplified note, a primer deck and a recall deck. Optionally: a cram sheet, fill-in-the-blank, written test and a podcast — build them at import or add them later in a tap.</div></details>
    <details class="qa"><summary>Do I have to build everything at once?</summary><div class="a">No. Notes and cards are always made; the extras are optional, so you only build what you'll use. You can generate any extra mode later from the topic in one tap, and it's saved after that.</div></details>
    <details class="qa"><summary>Is importing free?</summary><div class="a">Your first lecture — and everything built from it — is free. Importing more lectures is a premium upgrade.</div></details>
  </div>
</div></section>

